# CODEOWNERS — who must review changes to what.
# Owners are auto-requested for review on any PR touching their paths.
# Last matching pattern wins, so put the most specific rules at the bottom.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <@handle or @org/team>

# Default owner for everything
*                       @{{OWNER}}

# Product docs — the PM owns these outright
/docs/product/          @{{OWNER}}
/docs/decisions/        @{{OWNER}}
/ROADMAP.md             @{{OWNER}}
/CHANGELOG.md           @{{OWNER}}

# Anything that changes how the repo itself runs
/.github/               @{{OWNER}}

# --- Add as the team grows ---
# /src/api/             @backend-team
# /src/ui/              @frontend-team
# /infra/               @platform-team
# /**/*.sql             @data-team
#
# Rule of thumb: paths where a wrong change is expensive get an owner.
# Don't map every folder — CODEOWNERS that requests six reviewers per PR
# gets ignored, and then it protects nothing.
